  "id": "ss.enemy.trapjaw",
  "name": "Trapjaw",
  "description": "The burrow's charger, and the jaws are what throws it. The first cut hung two short blades off a normal-sized body and the pair read as sticks lying beside a bug; this one is mostly jaws. Two long calipers curve out from a head shrunk to the hinge they need, and everything behind that hinge tapers away — so the silhouette is an open mouth travelling, which cannot be confused with the Lance's one solid dart. Drawn from above along +x, because the game turns this body to its heading and fixes the line at the brace rather than at the launch: a creature that has already picked its lane has to be visibly pointing down it. Front legs reach forward, rear legs trail back, middle pair straight out to the side — the load is on the front pair, which is where the throw comes from. The only ember on it is the two tips and the trigger hairs between them: the bright part is the part that is cocked. No `elite` variant on purpose — the marking only lands on wave-table bodies, and this one arrives in squads. Gameplay radius 10.",
